class.description:
[InputSettingsServer] is the settings domain [code]"input"[/code]: it stores the input options chosen by the player, loads them when the game starts and offers helpers that apply them. The settings resource is an [InputSettings]. The file is [code]user://settings/input.ini[/code] by default; as a single record it is never stored as CSV.
Three values have an engine target and take effect at once: [member InputSettings.emulate_mouse_from_touch], [member InputSettings.emulate_touch_from_mouse] and [member InputSettings.use_accumulated_input] (see [Input]). Their defaults are the values the engine has when the domain starts, so they follow the project settings.
All other values (sensitivity, inversion, deadzone, smoothing, vibration, toggle actions, first player) have no engine target ([constant SettingsServer.SETTING_FLAG_NO_ENGINE_TARGET]): no engine API reads them, and [Input] is never changed, so the GUI and games that scale on their own are not affected. The game applies them through the helpers of this class, which read the pending values, so a slider in an options menu takes effect while it is dragged. Connect to [signal SettingsServer.value_changed] to react to a change.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
extends CharacterBody3D

func _ready():
	InputSettingsServer.set_mouse_captured(true)

func _unhandled_input(event):
	if event is InputEventMouseMotion:
		var look = InputSettingsServer.apply_to_mouse_motion(event.screen_relative)
		rotate_y(-look.x * 0.002)
		$Camera3D.rotate_x(-look.y * 0.002)

func _physics_process(delta):
	var stick = Input.get_vector("look_left", "look_right", "look_up", "look_down", 0.0)
	var look = InputSettingsServer.apply_to_stick(stick)
	rotate_y(-look.x * 3.0 * delta)
	var crouching = InputSettingsServer.is_action_active("crouch")
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public partial class Player : CharacterBody3D
{
    public override void _Ready()
    {
        InputSettingsServer.SetMouseCaptured(true);
    }

    public override void _UnhandledInput(InputEvent @event)
    {
        if (@event is InputEventMouseMotion motion)
        {
            Vector2 look = InputSettingsServer.ApplyToMouseMotion(motion.ScreenRelative);
            RotateY(-look.X * 0.002f);
            GetNode<Camera3D>("Camera3D").RotateX(-look.Y * 0.002f);
        }
    }

    public override void _PhysicsProcess(double delta)
    {
        Vector2 stick = Input.GetVector("look_left", "look_right", "look_up", "look_down", 0.0f);
        Vector2 look = InputSettingsServer.ApplyToStick(stick);
        RotateY(-look.X * 3.0f * (float)delta);
        bool crouching = InputSettingsServer.IsActionActive("crouch");
    }
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] In C#, the static class [code skip-lint]InputSettingsServer[/code] only has the methods of this class. The methods of [SettingsServer] are called through [code]InputSettingsServer.Singleton[/code].
[b]Note:[/b] Key bindings are not part of this domain.

method.description:
Returns the look input of [param event] with the settings applied: for an [InputEventMouseMotion], [method apply_to_mouse_motion] of its [member InputEventMouseMotion.screen_relative]; for an [InputEventJoypadMotion] of the right stick, [method apply_to_stick] of the whole right stick of its device. Returns [constant Vector2.ZERO] for all other events.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _unhandled_input(event):
	var look = InputSettingsServer.get_look_vector(event)
	rotate_y(-look.x * 0.002)
	$Camera3D.rotate_x(-look.y * 0.002)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _UnhandledInput(InputEvent @event)
{
    Vector2 look = InputSettingsServer.GetLookVector(@event);
    RotateY(-look.X * 0.002f);
    GetNode<Camera3D>("Camera3D").RotateX(-look.Y * 0.002f);
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] A joypad gives a position, not a motion: for smooth turning, read the stick every frame with [method apply_to_stick] instead.
